# The step of a for-in has just asked the object for its structure and its order word, or knows from the turn before that nothing has run; it says up to which name the enumerator's names are current. The test in front of the read under
# the key asked cell, structure and order word once more. f1 = straight: nothing stands between the step and the read: the test is handed the step's own count and holds the index of the name against it: the object is not touched.
# f2 = behindACall: other code has run since the step: the test asks the object as before. f3 = twice: the first read may run code of a compiled object's getter: the second test asks the object.
# RUN(STRAIGHT): walk f1:Body mechanisms=all
# STRAIGHT: [[step]]: {{*}} = ForInStep
# STRAIGHT: [[count]]: {{*}} = ResultAt [[step]] index=3
# STRAIGHT: IsEnumeratorCurrent {{*}}, {{*}}, {{*}}, [[count]] traits
# STRAIGHT: EnumeratorGetByVal
# RUN(CALL): walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
# CALL-NOT: IsEnumeratorCurrent {{*}}, {{*}}, {{*}}, {{*}} traits
# CALL: EnumeratorGetByVal
# RUN(ANSWERS): run-in-shell mechanisms=all
